    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4948e2a3-40f0-5dd0-b867-067dc6b12972",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 2 \\sqrt{1 - \\left(y - 5\\right)^{2}}$ for $\\,|\\left(y-5\\right)|<1.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 2 \\sqrt{1 - \\left(y - 5\\right)^{2}} \\\\ (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y - 5\\right)^{2}}})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y - 5\\right)^{2}}})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y - 5\\right)^{2}}})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y - 5\\right)^{2}}})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\arcsin{\\left(y - 5 \\right)} & =- 2 x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\arcsin{\\left(y - 5 \\right)}=- 2 x+C.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
