      ":question/id": "852b352d-ebe9-53fc-b7fd-5799d3696dab",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{9 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}}{\\cos{\\left(y - 6 \\right)}}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{9 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}}{\\cos{\\left(y - 6 \\right)}} \\\\ (\\cos{\\left(y - 6 \\right)})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =9 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\cos{\\left(y - 6 \\right)})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (9 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\cos{\\left(y - 6 \\right)})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (9 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\cos{\\left(y - 6 \\right)})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (9 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\sin{\\left(y - 6 \\right)} & =3 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(y - 6 \\right)}=3 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}+C.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
