      ":question/id": "e23ecbca-e598-5891-a05b-8e42f07c2af9",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\left(6 x - 18\\right) e^{1 - y}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\left(6 x - 18\\right) e^{1 - y} \\\\ (e^{y - 1})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6 x - 18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (e^{y - 1})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6 x - 18)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (e^{y - 1})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (6 x - 18)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (e^{y - 1})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (6 x - 18)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ e^{y - 1} & =- 6 x + 3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2} + 12+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ne^{y - 1}=- 6 x + 3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2} + 12+C.\n$$",
