      ":question/id": "afb7c269-d4ab-5113-9641-70a8f76fb892",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\left(y - 4\\right) \\sin{\\left(x + 1 \\right)}$ for $\\left(y-4\\right)\\ne 0.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\left(y - 4\\right) \\sin{\\left(x + 1 \\right)} \\\\ (\\frac{1}{y - 4})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sin{\\left(x + 1 \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{y - 4})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\sin{\\left(x + 1 \\right)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{y - 4})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (\\sin{\\left(x + 1 \\right)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{y - 4})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (\\sin{\\left(x + 1 \\right)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln{\\left(\\left|{y - 4}\\right| \\right)} & =- \\cos{\\left(x + 1 \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln{\\left(\\left|{y - 4}\\right| \\right)}=- \\cos{\\left(x + 1 \\right)}+C.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
